Task: reason-constants (track aguihitl_20260908, todo 2/20)

Summary
Added the AG-UI core interrupt reason constants (tool_call, input_required,
confirmation) and a CallName field on interrupt.Record recording which ADK
FunctionCall produced the interrupt, with ADKCallName/IsInputRequest helpers
for resume dispatch.

Files
- agui/internal/interrupt/interrupt.go (modified)
- agui/internal/interrupt/reason_test.go (created)

Why
The track spec originally dispatched resume on Record.Reason. That is wrong:
FR2 lets a host classifier return any custom reason string, so the reason
cannot identify which ADK call to answer. Persisting the call name makes the
dispatch unambiguous. Empty CallName means a record written before this
change, which was necessarily a tool confirmation, so it defaults there and
old sessions keep resuming correctly.

Verification
go build ./... clean; go vet ./agui/... clean; CI=true go test ./agui/... all
packages ok.
